# A USB device waiting to be proxied may also present a network adapter:
# phones, drones and modems do (RNDIS, ECM, NCM). Until the proxy takes the
# device over, the Pi is its USB host and would bring that interface up.
# The device under test would then share a network with the Pi and its web
# UI, and its DHCP server could change the Pi's routes.
#
# So mark every network interface that sits on a USB device as unmanaged:
# NetworkManager leaves it down, with no address. The Ethernet and Wi-Fi
# built into the Pi 4 and Pi 5 are not USB devices and are not affected.
#
# To use a USB Ethernet or Wi-Fi adapter with the Pi itself, switch this rule
# off with an empty file of the same name in /etc, then reboot:
#   sudo touch /etc/udev/rules.d/84-midwire-usb-net.rules
ACTION!="remove", SUBSYSTEM=="net", SUBSYSTEMS=="usb", ENV{NM_UNMANAGED}="1"
